            "date_modified": "2025-09-20T07:25:01.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-20T07:22:57.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "mfuji09",
                "url": "https://github.com/mfuji09"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 removed support for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/afterscriptexecute_event\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">afterscriptexecute</code> event in <code class=\"notranslate\">Document</code></a>, <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/afterscriptexecute_event\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">afterscriptexecute</code> event in <code class=\"notranslate\">Element</code></a>, <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/beforescriptexecute_event\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">beforescriptexecute</code> event in <code class=\"notranslate\">Document</code></a>, <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/beforescriptexecute_event\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">beforescriptexecute</code> event in <code class=\"notranslate\">Element</code></a> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1584269\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1584269</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417438266\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41141\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41141/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41141\">#41141</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41207",
            "title": "FF144 Relnote: beforescriptexecute and afterscriptexecute removal",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-19T05:57:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-19T05:55:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a new page to our list of \"attacks\", this one is on Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR).</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Developing a series of guides about common attacks on websites, explaining for each attack: how it works, the impact, and how to defend against it.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Need to hear what <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/wbamberg/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/wbamberg\">@wbamberg</a> has to say about this :)</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">None?</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41200",
            "title": "Add a page for IDOR attacks",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-29T09:35:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-18T13:38:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I noticed that all the other major sections of MDN (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, etc.) have a top-level self-link at the top of their sidebars. This PR does the same thing for Learn web development.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41195",
            "title": "Add top-level self-link to the learnsidebar",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-18T08:34:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-18T08:33:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6711831?u=81971bd9ebd5f5a68ca0e7646bb4f0736871b4f5&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds the missing Description Kind entry and writeup to the article.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This page elaborates more the elements but its always been missing the Description kind, other pages do contain it but not here, so for the sake of consistency and completeness, it should be added in..</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLTrackElement/kind\" rel=\"nofollow\">Here's a different page where it exists</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41190",
            "title": "Missing the Descriptions kind on <track>'s article",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-28T16:49:26.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-18T04:06:58.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "blizzard318",
                "url": "https://github.com/blizzard318"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28312.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1830235065\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/28312\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/28312/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/28312\">#28312</a>. This has the nice effect of getting rid of \"how-to\" guides in ARIA, because currently this one is extremely thin and isn't even a guide. The placement of the doc is tentative, because I can't find a better place for general web stuff.</p>",
